describe('/meters', () => {
  // this should work, but Cypress cookie handling is bugged, see:
  // https://github.com/cypress-io/cypress/issues/2515
  // beforeEach( () => {
  //   cy.login('mgm')
  // })

  it('retrieves booked meters as an account manager', () => {
    // this works, but now I have to login inside every single it() block
    cy.login('mgm', (response) => { 
      const options = {
        filter: ['parent_id', 'null'],
        fields: ['real-properties', 'id,name,installation-complete'],
        include: 'booked-meters,booked-meter-modules'
      }

      cy.api('GET', 'users', options, authToken).then( (response) => {
        cy.log(response)
      })
    })
  })
})
```

Ideally, for sending authenticated API requests (as seen in the above example) - we would need only to login during the beforeEach block and not need to wrap our api tests inside a login callback every time.

